What this means for openccu-loom users
-------------------------------------

Running the stock binary for personal home automation is explicitly
allowed. Commercial redistribution (e.g. bundling openccu-loom into a
paid product or paid hosted service) requires you to either:

  (a) obtain an eQ-3 license for the embedded extracts, or
  (b) replace the embedded data with self-extracted or otherwise
      licensed artifacts by pointing cfg.CCUData.*_path at the
      alternate files. The daemon's load order is
      (config-path) → (embedded) → (empty), so the override is a
      drop-in swap.

Refreshing the archives
-----------------------

Run `make update-ccu-data` to resync from a local openccu-data
checkout. See docs/adr/0003-embed-occu-extracts.md for the rationale
and the dependency graph.
